# The owner approves every change to these paths (factory/CONFIG.md, merge rule): CI and
# release automation, the release tree and the installer, the workspace manifests and
# lockfiles, and the factory's rules and designs: its product file, its values, its process,
# the role files that define when pm may merge without the owner, and the RFCs that
# exception rests on. Branch protection on main and v2 requires a code owner's review, so a
# pull request that touches one of them cannot be merged by an agent, and no agent can widen
# its own merge rights. The decision log in factory/decisions/ stays out, so pm can merge a
# decided RFC's implementation together with the engine-internal decisions it records.

